 ### 5. Operations & Geometric Features (`tools.rs`, `pick.rs`, `area.rs`, `features.rs`, #180, #312)
 - `list_operation_types {}`: Inspect all supported operation types, parameter schemas, defaults, and compatible tool types.
 - `add_operation { "kind": string, "tool"?: string, "name"?: string, "source"?: string, "params"?: object }`: Add an operation to the active setup. `source` is `"stock"` (the default), a model name, or the name of a placed DXF profile (#1862: 2D milling, plasma and wire EDM kinds only; a kind that needs a solid model refuses a profile by name, and a 3D kind refuses a setup that has only a stock and a profile). `tool` is required for every kind where `list_operation_types` lists `"mounts_tool": true` (including `Wire Contour` with a `Wire` tool such as `"EDM-W025"`); only a kind with `"mounts_tool": false` omits `"tool"`.
-- **Wire Contour (#532, #1108, #2011)**: a 2-axis, constant-taper, or 4-axis wire EDM cut of one closed profile (a model's through silhouette or picked edges) or an open run (`side: "left"|"right"`). Mount a wire EDM first: built-in `"Sodick ALC400G"` or `"AGIECUT Classic 2S (template)"` via `load_machine { "builtin": "..." }` (plus `edit_machine` to add `edm.conditions` and any `edm.codes`), or `load_machine { "path": "<.mch>" }` with an `edm.conditions` table. Add a `Wire` tool (`add_tool { "catalog": "EDM-W025", "holder": "none" }`, or a custom tool with `kind: "wire"`, `diameter` 0.02-1.0 mm, `rpm: 0`). Then `add_operation { "kind": "Wire Contour", "tool": "EDM-W025", "source": "<model>", "params": { "condition": "<condition id>", "side": "die"|"punch"|"left"|"right", "start": [x, y] } }`. All fields (`list_operation_types { "kind": "wire_contour" }`): `top_z`, `bottom_z`, `condition`, `side`, `start`, `tabs`, `capture`, `taper_deg`, `burnout_clearance`, `clearance`, `skims`, `four_axis`, `sharp_corners`; `edit_operation` patches any of them. Refusals arrive as tool errors in the command's words: missing or non-wire tool, no or unknown condition, a condition with no gap or wire diameter, or `taper_deg` past `edm.max_taper_deg`; the start hole and the corner minimum are refused at `generate`. Post with `"Generic ISO Wire EDM"` (vertical, skims, constant taper, and 4-axis via `edm.codes`), `"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)"` (vertical 2-axis only; refuses taper and 4-axis), or `"Native wire EDM job files"` (a native controller job directory for `"AGIECUT Classic 2S (template)"` with condition `AGIE_QN2`, one straight-sided vertical punch (`source: "<model>"`, `side: "punch"`) in 15, 20, 40 or 80 mm stock, or one convex die opening (`side: "die"`, the picked edge chains of the upper rim through `set_operation_geometry`) in a 20 mm plate, and 0.25 mm wire; punch reentrant corners are checked, not refused: each inside corner must be reached by the rough offset of the selected thickness within 0.002 mm, every segment must hold both corner joins, nonadjacent faces must keep the swept rough passes apart, and the entry must be on a straight exterior face; a notch that fails these checks is refused, see `docs/decisions/2956-agie-reentrant-punch.md` and `docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md`); milling posts refuse wire cuts by name. Neither built-in wire `.mch` ships with `edm.conditions`, and the wire posts are not exercised on a physical EDM control.
+- **Wire Contour (#532, #1108, #2011)**: a 2-axis, constant-taper, or 4-axis wire EDM cut of one closed profile (a model's through silhouette or picked edges) or an open run (`side: "left"|"right"`). Mount a wire EDM first: built-in `"Sodick ALC400G"` or `"AGIECUT Classic 2S (template)"` via `load_machine { "builtin": "..." }` (plus `edit_machine` to add `edm.conditions` and any `edm.codes`), or `load_machine { "path": "<.mch>" }` with an `edm.conditions` table. Add a `Wire` tool (`add_tool { "catalog": "EDM-W025", "holder": "none" }`, or a custom tool with `kind: "wire"`, `diameter` 0.02-1.0 mm, `rpm: 0`). Then `add_operation { "kind": "Wire Contour", "tool": "EDM-W025", "source": "<model>", "params": { "condition": "<condition id>", "side": "die"|"punch"|"left"|"right", "picks": { "start": [[x, y]] } } }`. All fields (`list_operation_types { "kind": "wire_contour" }`): `top_z`, `bottom_z`, `condition`, `side`, `picks`, `tabs`, `capture`, `taper_deg`, `burnout_clearance`, `clearance`, `skims`, `four_axis`, `sharp_corners`; `edit_operation` patches any of them. Refusals arrive as tool errors in the command's words: missing or non-wire tool, no or unknown condition, a condition with no gap or wire diameter, or `taper_deg` past `edm.max_taper_deg`; the start hole and the corner minimum are refused at `generate`. Post with `"Generic ISO Wire EDM"` (vertical, skims, constant taper, and 4-axis via `edm.codes`), `"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)"` (vertical 2-axis only; refuses taper and 4-axis), or `"Native wire EDM job files"` (a native controller job directory for `"AGIECUT Classic 2S (template)"` with condition `AGIE_QN2`, one straight-sided vertical punch (`source: "<model>"`, `side: "punch"`) in 15, 20, 40 or 80 mm stock, or one convex die opening (`side: "die"`, the picked edge chains of the upper rim through `set_operation_geometry`) in a 20 mm plate, and 0.25 mm wire; punch reentrant corners are checked, not refused: each inside corner must be reached by the rough offset of the selected thickness within 0.002 mm, every segment must hold both corner joins, nonadjacent faces must keep the swept rough passes apart, and the entry must be on a straight exterior face; a notch that fails these checks is refused, see `docs/decisions/2956-agie-reentrant-punch.md` and `docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md`); milling posts refuse wire cuts by name. Neither built-in wire `.mch` ships with `edm.conditions`, and the wire posts are not exercised on a physical EDM control.
 - **Sinker electrode (#547, #1156)**: `electrode_from_faces { "name": string, "picks": [face ids], "undersize"?: number, "condition"?: string, "setup"?: string, "orbit"?: number, "stub": number, "pickup": number }` generates a sinker EDM electrode from the picked faces of a cavity (its level floor and every vertical wall standing on it, `face:0x…` ids from `list_features`, all on one model) and adds it as a document tool. Give `undersize` (mm per side, 0 or more) or `condition` (a machine EDM condition id, read from the setup's sinker EDM; `setup` names that setup, default the active one), not both; `stub` (more than 0) is how far the electrode stands above the cavity's mouth; `pickup` (0 or more) is the offset from the electrode's top to the measuring reference. `orbit` makes it that much smaller again per side. The reply gives the electrode, its `burn` fields (the `add_operation` params of a Sinker Burn of this cavity) a `warning` when the stated undersize is 0 (the electrode is then the cavity's full size, so any spark gap burns the walls past it), and a `note` when an orbit is given. Only an axis-aligned rectangular cavity yields an electrode; refused by name: picks on more than one model or on something that is not a face, a degenerate face, a boss, rib or overhang standing in the electrode's way, a condition with no undersize or no sinker EDM setup, a model whose facets can't be read, and malformed numbers. One undo step.
 - `edit_operation { "name": string, "params": object }`: JSON merge-patch operation parameters (e.g. `stepdown`, `stepover`, `feed`, `spindle_speed`).
 - **Change a lead shape (#2876)**: `add_operation` and `edit_operation` merge object keys, including enum shape keys. Inspect the current shape with `get_job`, or the seeded defaults with `list_operation_types`. To change a linear lead to an arc, give `"params": { "lead": { "linear": null, "arc": { "radius": 3.0 } } }`. Remove the old key with `null` in the same patch. For a nested lead, give `"params": { "links": { "approach": { "lead_out": { "linear": null, "arc": { "radius": 3.0 } } } } }`. Without removal, the refusal keeps the parser error and lists the merged field paths and keys, such as `lead: arc, linear`.
